      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When those little air sprites get interrupted or start acting up, that's when things go from smooth flight to a messy, chaotic mess, much like when a swarm of tiny, unpredictable gnats gets into a perfectly organized line of march. If the flow separates—if the sprites suddenly decide to stop following the curve of the wing and start tumbling into random eddies—that's called airflow separation. This separation is a big problem because it destroys the smooth pressure difference your wing relies on, causing a sudden, dramatic loss of lift.",
